findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config_loading tests and dev implementation don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA listed ''CWE-209: Error messages don''t leak internal paths, tokens,
    or stack traces'' as a security test in cli_error_exit_codes.rs. Reviewer also
    noted sanitize_error_body limitations but did not flag the Display impl leak specifically.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-113 header injection tests in siem_client.rs covering CRLF\
    \ in token/tenant values. However, the Reviewer flagged that with_token()/with_tenant()\
    \ bypass validation, meaning the unchecked path still exists. Partially caught\
    \ \u2014 the risk was identified but the raw String type vs TenantId issue was\
    \ not."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on ClientConfigFile (config.rs:7),
    and Reviewer verified it. This prevents silent acceptance of unknown fields like
    token.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in tests. The Reviewer noted a dead Ok branch in a different test but not
    this specific vacuous assertion.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via let _ = config.
